Article 48
(1) Regional Government in efforts to fulfill children's rights is responsible for:
a. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the fulfillment of children's rights;
b. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every child without discriminating based on ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnic group, culture and language, legal status of the child, birth order of the child, and physical and/or mental condition;
c. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for improving family quality in realizing children's rights;
d. guaranteeing the protection, care and welfare of children by taking into account the rights and obligations of parents, guardians or other persons who are legally responsible for the child;
e. guaranteeing the right of children to express opinions in accordance with the age and level of intelligence of the child;
f. conducting supervision and guidance in the context of implementing the fulfillment of children's rights; and
g. conducting cooperation with private parties and/or NGOs in implementing child protection.
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in child protection efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the Regional Apparatus that administers Government Affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

