CHAPTER VIII
GENDER AND CHILD DATA SYSTEM
Article 70
Regional governments in order to provide protection for children:
a. conduct prevention of violence against children by optimizing the role of customary institutions;
b. conduct socialization seminars and counseling regarding child protection and rights;
c. develop child-friendly school models;
d. provide public facilities that are friendly and safe for children;
e. compile databases and information about acts of violence against children;
f. conduct mapping of locations and areas vulnerable to the occurrence of violence against children;
g. conduct coordination and cooperation in preventing violations of children's rights;
h. strengthen the function of institutions or organizations working in the field of child protection; and
i. encourage community awareness of the importance of child protection by establishing assistance for the protection of women and children.

