Article 66
(1) In the framework of fulfilling children's rights in an integrated, systematic and sustainable manner, the Regional Government establishes a Regional Action Plan for the Development of a Child-Friendly Regency.
(2) The Regional Action Plan for the Development of a Child-Friendly Regency as referred to in paragraph (1), contains:
a. the concept of a Child-Friendly Regency concerning objectives, strategies and the roles of related parties;
b. children's rights;
c. the approach to developing a Child-Friendly Regency.
Article 67
(1) The Regional Action Plan for the Development of a Child-Friendly Regency is directed at fulfilling children's rights which are divided into 5 (five) target groups, comprising:
a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, use of leisure time, cultural activities; and
e. special protection.
(2) Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan for the Development of a Child-Friendly Regency as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

